      "cell": 0,
      "text": "# ARC3 031 Recorded State Exact Pixels\n\nPrivate public-environment research. One GPU model load, 2 isolated\nharness process(es), 3 games per arm, requested\n600-second solver budgets. Total session hard\nlimit: 3600 seconds (1 hours).\nArm order: segmentation_forks_A, segmentation_forks_B. This notebook does not submit to the competition.\n\nPurpose: Isolated-process same-state comparison of 009 Python lifecycle versus exact segmentation runs; no program repair..\n\nBase: [Daniel Franzen Milestone 2 v3](https://www.kaggle.com/code/dfranzen/arc-agi-3-milestone-2-solution)\nand [Tufa Duck](https://github.com/Tufalabs/duck-harness). Original harness and\nserving code are retained with attribution; source repository license is\nApache-2.0. Model and third-party runtime licenses remain their own.\n\nBaseline first, candidate second, fresh CPU process and flushed model cache. Identical recorded frame/messages/functions; candidate only adds exact runs and field guidance. Diagnostic replay is not a natural full-pool score.\n"
    },
    {
      "cell": 15,
      "text": "## 0. Harness patch\n\nPatch to add our modifications to the original tufa harness."
    },
    {
      "cell": 17,
      "text": "## 1. Environment and submission mode\n\nDetect whether this is a real competition rerun (which minimises diagnostics), set the\nframework's environment flags, and put the CUDA libraries on the linker path."
    },
    {
      "cell": 19,
      "text": "## 2. Precaching\n\nPrecache wheelhouse for faster startup."
    },
    {
      "cell": 21,
      "text": "## 3. Install the ARC runtime\n\nInstall `arc-agi` from the offline competition wheelhouse (the Kaggle submission environment\nhas no internet)."
    },
    {
      "cell": 23,
      "text": "## 4. Import the bundled source\n\nPut the snapshotted repositories on the path (this process and any child processes)."
    },
    {
      "cell": 25,
      "text": "## 5. Start serving\n\nInstall and startup sglang to serve the model."
    }
  ],
